  "full_text": "First thing like a diagram of carbon molecules or carbon molecules anyway, I was just thinking about a So like growing up I had brothers and sisters and stuff right and like get the strange idea that in order for me to reproduce you have to have the same Configuration anyway, like like if you're gonna make Noah's Ark, what would it require? Like you would have to have the same If you had a sister growing up, you'd have to have something being the sister, and you'd have to have a brother or something like that. And the issue of black and white and big and small, maybe that ties into it. So like last night, you know there's something to be said about being autistic. Why? Because imagine you're snowbound. If you're snowbound in a house or something, or in a trench, or in war, they got a lot of time alone, right? If you can entertain yourself, that's good. Autism shouldn't be two things. Autism shouldn't be necessarily mocked. It's not necessarily a problem. And the other thing is brothers and sisters need to be included in... The whole model of society doesn't include the role of brothers and sisters anymore. So it's really messed up. so the the girls last night were kind of like sisters i guess or something like that but anyway so uh um so",
